  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-12-29T19:05:22.243Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "yt-dlp has a search feature that can retrieve the 'first match' for youtube videos. \n\nI recently implemented this into AICom and originally I was skeptical of it, thinking it would lead to a lot of abuse, or return bad results. \n\nBut surprisingly people are loving it, and it's working great. So I think what would work best for VRChat's video system is to do a fall back to searching for the video in the same way if the url is not an actual url.",
